&lt;p&gt;This role serves as the key analytics business partner for the Go-To-Market (GTM) organization, driving data-driven decision-making across the Sales, Marketing, Channel, and Post-Sales functions. The Senior GTM Analyst translates complex operational data into actionable insights to improve business predictability and optimize resource allocation. This position directly impacts the strategic investment decisions that yield the highest return across the entire Axonius customer journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead comprehensive &lt;strong&gt;performance deep dives&lt;/strong&gt; across all GTM functions (e.g., sales pipeline stages, campaign efficiency, channel partner efficacy, and customer retention/churn metrics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design, build, and maintain&lt;/strong&gt; standardized reporting infrastructure, dashboards, and templates using BI tools (e.g., Tableau) to establish a single source of truth for GTM Key Performance Indicators (KPIs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the development and refinement of &lt;strong&gt;Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR) and Sales Pipeline models&lt;/strong&gt; to enhance forecasting accuracy and business predictability for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop &lt;strong&gt;financial models&lt;/strong&gt; to assess GTM spend efficiency and support annual planning, including capacity planning and quarterly target-setting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
